/* Expected output: 1  0  7
 * Relational binds LOOSER than arithmetic. With a=1, b=2:
 *   a + 1 < b * 2   correct: (a+1)<(b*2) = 2<4 = 1     wrong: a+(1<b)*2 = 3
 *   a + 1 > b * 2   correct: 2>4 = 0                    wrong: a+(1>b)*2 = 1
 * Each result differs under the wrong grouping, so this test cannot pass
 * by accident. The last line checks * binds tighter than + and -. */
int main() {
    int a; int b;
    a = 1; b = 2;
    print(a + 1 < b * 2);
    print(a + 1 > b * 2);
    print(2 + 3 * 4 - 7);
    return 0;
}
